WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.010
February.

2
00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:06.150
An easterly wind sets in, and snow
showers sweep in near the east coast.

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:10.710
On such nights, it is often
below minus 10 degrees Celsius.

4
00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:11.630
July.

5
00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:15.370
A south-easterly blows
in, and it's hot and hazy:

6
00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:18.550
often over 30 degrees Celsius by day.

7
00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:23.310
The record temperatures of August
2003 came in air like this.

8
00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:26.290
So why can wind from the
east bring snow in winter,

9
00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:28.490
but a heatwave in summer?

10
00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:31.290
In this mission, you'll find
out what an air mass is,

11
00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:33.190
and decode its name.

12
00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:36.910
Then you'll match each one to
its winter and summer weather.

13
00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:42.010
Your mission: explain why an easterly wind
brings snow in February but a heatwave

14
00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:43.000
in July.
